<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chidambaram</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chidambaram is a temple town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tamil-nadu">Tamil Nadu</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coromandel-coast">Coromandel</a> coast. It is famous for the Thillai <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nataraja">Nataraja</a> Temple, dedicated to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiva">Shiva</a> as the cosmic dancer Nataraja, one of the most sacred sites of Tamil <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shaivism">Shaivism</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Chola</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandya-dynasty">Pandya</a> and later kings endowed and enlarged the temple, whose gilded hall and great gateway towers date from many periods.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chidambaram.jpg" alt="Chidambaram" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ryan · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chidambaram_Temple.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
